KNOWN GAP found while testing T6: Ir.load_theory (ir.ML) refuses to run
whenever Ir.is_interactive_session () is true, which reads
Printer.show_markup_default -- a flag meant to distinguish jEdit from
batch `isabelle build`. Our MCP_Session backend runs a Headless.Session,
which goes through the same init_options_interactive as jEdit and sets
that ref true. Consequence: load_theory cannot run from the live MCP
server at all today, and since repl_init's "Thy:idx" segment spec
requires a theory loaded with record_theories (only load_theory does
that), that spec form is unusable end to end until this is fixed. Pinned
as a regression test (isabelle mcp_test -b: "KNOWN GAP -- load_theory
refuses to run from a headless MCP_Session") so a fix is forced to
update it. Belongs to plans/load_theory's scope to actually fix
(distinguish "headless server" from "interactive jEdit", not just
"batch build" from "interactive"); flagging here since T6 discovered it.
